WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:14.080
The war on drugs was crushed on Election&nbsp;
Day, at least as much as you could crush it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:21.360
in one day. In every state where marijuana&nbsp;
legalization or decriminalization or progressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:27.840
ization of drug policy was on the ballot, it won&nbsp;
in Arizona, Montana, New Jersey and South Dakota,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:36.800
voters legalized recreational marijuana.&nbsp;
Incredible in Mississippi and even South Dakota&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:44.080
voters legalized medical marijuana. South Dakota&nbsp;
had both legalized recreational and legalized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:52.400
medical. In Oregon, voters decriminalized but not&nbsp;
legalized all drugs, including cocaine and heroin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.880
Also in Oregon, voters legalized the&nbsp;
use of psilocybin, a psychedelic drug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.800
found in so-called magic mushrooms in&nbsp;
specifically supervised therapeutic uses.&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:10.240
This is huge. Oregon also is. So what's going to&nbsp;
happen in Oregon is you will no longer be punished&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.440
with jail or prison time for small amounts of&nbsp;
possession of any drug that includes cocaine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.160
and heroin. If you get caught with cocaine and&nbsp;
heroin, you can either pay a hundred dollars fine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.160
or do a completed health assessment, the details&nbsp;
of which I don't yet know. But we will find out.&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:32.240
In Washington, D.C., voters decriminalized&nbsp;
psychedelic plants also following following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:39.120
the lead of several other cities. And again,&nbsp;
Oregon, the first state in the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:48.640
in modern times to decriminalize all drugs.&nbsp;
Marijuana is now legalized in 15 states, plus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.040
Washington, D.C., although Washington, D.C.&nbsp;
still does not allow sales, all measures won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.760
by at least five percentage points in every&nbsp;
state. This really is not hugely shocking.&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:08.000
Over the last decade, we've seen polls show&nbsp;
marijuana legalization is increasingly popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.840
in many polls. Even among Republicans, there is&nbsp;
support for at least marijuana decriminalization.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.680
This is a big rejection of the war on drugs.&nbsp;
It starts to signal a major shift in U.S. drug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.800
policy. It's going to push for more of the&nbsp;
disassembly of the war on drugs. But another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:30.640
thing that's important to remember is we are&nbsp;
getting the first steps here, but we still need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:36.800
to deal with the criminal justice component.&nbsp;
So, for example, if anybody has a record now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:44.000
for in Oregon, if you have a record for possession&nbsp;
of small amounts of cocaine, which now are legal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.880
decriminalized, I should say, not legalize&nbsp;
decriminalized, what happens to your record?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.680
It should probably be expunged. And that is the&nbsp;
next step. That is the next step here. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.880
the next forefront. Legal cannabis. You know, nice&nbsp;
for people looking to go to a nice store and get,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:05.920
you know, curated, curated pot. But the criminal&nbsp;
justice piece is more difficult and it has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.400
come right after this. And hopefully we will&nbsp;
see that. Also, I expect to see the tobacco&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.120
industry get more and more into cannabis.
And there's also real opportunities in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.280
terms of taking the tax revenue that this will&nbsp;
generate and really doing great things with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.840
We're going to be discussing it more. We're&nbsp;
going to be looking to places like Colorado,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:30.000
even Massachusetts, as potential models of how&nbsp;
this can be managed, how the money can be used.&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.880
But a major win against the war on drugs&nbsp;
on Tuesday. And we'll keep talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.480
ballot initiatives because there's a lot&nbsp;
of really interesting stuff to discuss.

